WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.759
He sold his happiest memory to a

00:00:01.799 --> 00:00:05.599
stranger behind a counter. You see,

00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:07.519
memories are money here. There's a shop

00:00:05.599 --> 00:00:09.319
on every corner that'll pull one right

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:11.399
out of your skull. Landlords take rent

00:00:09.319 --> 00:00:13.039
in birthdays and a bag of groceries cost

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:15.560
the day you learn to ride a bike. The

00:00:13.039 --> 00:00:17.440
city is split in two by a giant wall. On

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.440
one side, the rich just buy everyone

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.479
else's summers. So, some guy over there

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.000
has been to the Bahamas 300 times

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:24.879
without leaving his couch. On the other

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.399
side, people stare at old photos of

00:00:24.879 --> 00:00:29.280
themselves smiling with no idea why. And

00:00:27.399 --> 00:00:30.799
since the rich only want the good stuff,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.750
the happier the memory, the more it

00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:34.319
pays. Jerry only sold his to cover

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.319
[music] rent, but that same week his

00:00:34.319 --> 00:00:38.240
little brother gets sick and every night

00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:39.919
in the hospital he begs for the same

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.959
bedtime story. The summer they caught a

00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:43.639
frog the size of a football at the lake.

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:45.639
But the medicine costs way more than

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:47.400
rent. So, Jerry goes back and sells that

00:00:45.639 --> 00:00:49.040
summer for a week of it. The best

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.000
birthday he ever had pays for the

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.759
surgery. And soon he's selling whole

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.720
years until [music] his head is mostly

00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:56.560
bad days and bus rides. His brother

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.319
keeps getting worse until there's only

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.260
one good year left. And the guy behind

00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:02.000
the counter stares at him and says, "Kid

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.959
[music], you sell this, there's nothing

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.199
happy left in there." He sells it anyway

00:01:03.959 --> 00:01:08.160
and it pays for everything. A week later

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:10.040
his brother sits up in bed cured [music]

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.319
and says, "Hey Jerry, tell me the frog

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.559
story." And Jerry has no idea who this

00:01:12.319 --> 00:01:16.919
kid is. He sold [music] every happy year

00:01:14.559 --> 00:01:19.760
he ever had and his brother was in every

00:01:16.919 --> 00:01:19.760
single one.

